    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0350" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.34/9–2846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Messersmith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-11-06T18:00:00-05:00">November 6, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1340. Urdes 876 Sept 28.<anchor n="39"
                        xml:id="d265-f1"/> Dept considers release of four demilitarized frigates
                    would seriously prejudice continuation of embargo agreement with British. These
                    vessels are unsuited commercial uses <pb facs="0351" n="333" xml:id="pg333"/>
                    and easily rearmed. Export license accordingly denied Sept 18 pending further
                    clarification compliance problem.</p>
                <p>Dept concurs your recommendation re Victory ships (urtel 2372 Nov 4<anchor n="39a" xml:id="d265-f2"/>). However, only
                    application so far received by Maritime from Flota<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d265-f3"/> is for three regular Victory ships for cargo purposes.
                    Navy unaware objection cited urtel.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
